1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:14.000
What happens to people who never heard of Jesus? If Jesus is the only way to the Father, what about a man born in a remote village who died without ever hearing his name?

2
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:32.000
People ask this in our comments all the time, so let's allow the Bible to answer it. In Caesarea, there lived a Roman officer named Cornelius, a Gentile who had never heard the gospel preached.

3
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Yet the Bible says he feared God with all his house, gave much to the poor, and prayed to God continually.

4
00:00:47.000 --> 00:01:02.000
One afternoon, an angel told him to send for a man called Peter, who was lodging by the sea in Joppa.

5
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:18.000
When Peter walked into that house, he said, "God is no respecter of persons, but in every nation he that feareth him is accepted with him."

6
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:30.000
So the first answer is this. God saw a man reaching for him with the little light he had, and he sent the gospel straight to his door.

7
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:46.000
The second answer is that no one is born without any light at all. Paul writes that God's eternal power is clearly seen in creation, and that his law is written on the hearts of people who never had the scriptures.

8
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:58.000
When Paul walked through Athens, he found an altar carved with the words, "To the unknown God," built by people reaching for a God they couldn't name.

9
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:12.000
The third answer is that God will judge every person fairly by what they were given. Jesus said, "Unto whomsoever much is given, of him shall be much required."

10
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Centuries earlier, Abraham pleaded with God for the city of Sodom and asked, "Shall not the judge of all the earth do right?" God agreed to spare the whole city if even 10 righteous people could be found inside it.

11
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Christians still disagree on exactly how God deals with those who never heard. Some believe a person must hear of Jesus and trust him in this life, while others believe Christ can save people who never learned his name. But every one of those views agrees that no one is saved except through Jesus.

12
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Then Paul asks a question that puts the weight back on our shoulders.

